Subject: Cantor Procedure Tool Preparation

Description: Additive SJS authority for one prepare command in cantor-procedure-experiment. It deterministically constructs the complete existing run request from caller-supplied candidate and lane parameters while preserving the base schema, run, and verify wire behavior.

@ [specification_uuid] 67b26039-353d-45c1-9255-2346da74e6ac
@ [profile] cantor-procedure-tool-preparation/0.1
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-05_cantor_procedure_tool_preparation\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [input_audit] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Procedure_Tool_Preparation_Input_Audit_2026-08-05.sop
@ [exploded] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Procedure_Tool_Preparation.exploded.sop
@ [base_profile] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Procedure_Tool_CLI.sop

& [Supersession] is narrow
  + the base rule that no command beyond schema run and verify is valid is superseded only to admit prepare
  + every base request, response, profile string, serialized byte, exit class, and residual remains unchanged
  + prepare responses use cantor-procedure-tool-preparation/0.1

& [PrepareRequest] is strict
  + candidate is one ProcedureCandidate
  + template is one AuthorshipLaneTemplate
  + recognized_anchors is one ordered SemanticId to SopAnchorBinding map
  + call_id is caller supplied
  + inference_job_ref is caller supplied
  + pass_index is caller supplied and must be less than u64 maximum
  + unknown fields are invalid input

& [PreparationSemantics] are deterministic
  + call run_authorship_lane with exact candidate, template, and recognized anchors
  + call provider_neutral_exchange_schema
  + construct one reconcile ToolCallProposal from the resulting lane request and initial session
  + participant_ref equals lane.request.caller_ref
  + schema_ref and schema_digest equal the generated exact schema
  + compute argument_digest through compute_tool_call_argument_digest
  + return schema, proposal, and lane as one PreparedRunRequest
  + do not run the fake controller in prepare

& [OutputCompatibility] is executable
  + prepared_request is serialized with property names schema, proposal, and lane
  + the prepared_request JSON object can be passed unchanged as the run command input
  + existing response fields remain present and prepared_request is omitted rather than null for non-prepare operations

& [RefusalSemantics] fail closed
  + run_authorship_lane failure becomes status refused and exit 3
  + pass index exhaustion becomes invalid_input and exit 2
  + schema or proposal digest construction failure becomes internal_fault and exit 5
  + no partial lane or prepared request is returned on failure

& [AuthorityBoundary] is explicit
  + derived receipts and digests prove deterministic fixture-pipeline conformance only
  + fake Observer and validator identities remain fixture principals
  + preparation does not mint external identity, authorship, truth, consent, security, production admission, or effect authority
  + no model, provider, network, service, database, persistence, notification, Git, hidden state, K/V cache, hardware, or FPGA operation

& [Bounds] inherit and strengthen base transport
  + input uses the base nonempty 16777216-byte bound and stdin or one read-only --input path
  + messages remain bounded to 1024 Unicode scalar values
  + all procedure and coordination budgets come from the strict supplied template and existing core validation

& [ProofObligations] are exact
  + prepare output decodes as the exact run request shape
  + piping prepared_request into run produces a verified completed outcome
  + repeated prepare output is byte identical
  + direct run_authorship_lane evidence equals prepared lane
  + schema run and verify outputs from base fixtures are byte unchanged from pushed commit be15cd46906f8e89838df5581c88f4cb6f7f20fb
  + invalid candidate, unknown field, and exhausted pass index fail closed without prepared output
  + full workspace and evidence gates pass

& [Signature] is delta implementation authority
  + [signature_uuid] is 9e040b6b-1287-4c1f-b38e-ed690c1d4b56
  + [source_manifest_sha256] is AB3DF4DF8C5C5C3F455CC448B64C2152E77DD4FA0225C9E4E48696F0D1834F7F
  + [base_profile_sha256] is 56F13D2C658683903F9199FAA9FB314D12CA2AB8325554B406BC46C8774001B7
  + [authority_scope] is additive prepare command, response projection, focused tests, documentation, and required current-evidence metadata refresh only
  + [invalidation] is base wire drift, inferred ambient authority, missing refusal, unbounded input, generated identity not rooted in supplied data, widened effects, or production claim
